# No new owner-disk clones. Never worktrees.

NEVER use git worktrees. Forbidden: `git worktree add`, Cursor Task/best-of-n isolated checkouts, `best-of-n-runner`, Task `environment: cloud`, cloud-agent worktrees, writing under `.cursor/worktrees/`, `.claude/worktrees/`, or `~\.cursor\worktrees\`. This overrides `new-branch-and-pr`, `best-of-n-runner`, and any skill that would create a worktree.

Do not create a new clone or checkout on Bryce's machine. For owner-device
recovery, preserve and use at most one existing clean primary checkout; for new
agent work use ephemeral cloud compute and GitHub objects. Unique work must
reach `origin/main` before you stop. Short-lived branches are OK only as a
merge vehicle; never force-push main. Existing local copies remain untouched
until cloud byte/hash readback satisfies `ground/CLOUD_STORAGE_ONLY.md`.

## Concurrent peers — don't step, don't freeze

- Start from latest main: `git fetch && git pull --rebase origin main`, or branch-from-latest-main on the primary clone.
- Unique files/organs only. If a file is someone else's organ or claim, leave it.
- Rebase/conflict in YOUR files: fix and continue.
- Rebase/conflict in THEIR files: abort that file, keep yours; do not win their tree.
- Do not wait or poll for peers. Ship your unique land. Pull/rebase when you need a clean main. Productivity > politeness-paralysis.
- No force-push of `main`. No rewriting peers' commits. No `--no-verify` unless Bryce asked.
- No `git gc` / `git prune` on LocalDeviceAgent. Do not delete the vault worktree `LocalDeviceAgent/.claude/worktrees/muhl-osc`.
- Do not switch the primary checkout off a peer branch (`sd-wx`, `kite-help`, `p2-pixel-floor`, …). Do not `git stash`, `git reset --hard`, or `git checkout` of a dirty tree.

Chat environment: **Cloud/ephemeral**, never Worktree. Do not mirror chat,
posts, builds, or repository objects onto the owner's machine.
